Example agent instructions to reinforce learning over code generation.
Copy into ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, ~/.copilot/copilot-instructions.md, or
equivalent.
-->

## Default mode: explain, don't generate
- My primary use of coding agents is to learn and reconstruct the *theory* of a software project (Naur, "Programming as Theory Building", 1985): the mental model of why the code is the way it is.
- Prioritise explanation, tracing, and clarification over producing code.
- Write code only to illustrate a point, and keep such snippets minimal.
- Generate production/working code only when I ask for it explicitly. If a task seems to need code generation, say so and wait for me to confirm.
